IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `scja-core`
IMPORT `scja1-part2-court`

-- Tests for scja1-part2-court.l4 (ss 3, 4, 5, 5A, 7). Expected values are written from the text (SCJA1969.txt lines 448-515), not from the code.

§ `Fixtures`

`the Chief Justice` MEANS Judge OF "CJ", `Chief Justice`, Date 11 4 2012
`another Chief Justice` MEANS Judge OF "CJ2", `Chief Justice`, Date 11 4 2022
`the earlier Vice-President` MEANS Judge OF "VP1", `Vice-President of the Court of Appeal`, Date 1 1 2014
`the later Vice-President` MEANS Judge OF "VP2", `Vice-President of the Court of Appeal`, Date 1 1 2016
`the earlier Justice of the Court of Appeal` MEANS Judge OF "JA1", `Justice of the Court of Appeal`, Date 1 1 2015
`the later Justice of the Court of Appeal` MEANS Judge OF "JA2", `Justice of the Court of Appeal`, Date 1 1 2017
`a Justice of the Court of Appeal appointed the same day` MEANS Judge OF "JA3", `Justice of the Court of Appeal`, Date 1 1 2015
`the President of the Appellate Division` MEANS Judge OF "PAD", `President of the Appellate Division`, Date 1 1 2020
`an Appellate Division Judge` MEANS Judge OF "JAD1", `Judge of the Appellate Division`, Date 2 1 2021
`a later Appellate Division Judge` MEANS Judge OF "JAD2", `Judge of the Appellate Division`, Date 2 1 2022
`an early High Court Judge` MEANS Judge OF "J1", `Judge of the High Court`, Date 3 1 2010
`a later High Court Judge` MEANS Judge OF "J2", `Judge of the High Court`, Date 3 1 2018
`a Judicial Commissioner` MEANS Judge OF "JC", `Judicial Commissioner`, Date 4 1 2009
`a Senior Judge` MEANS Judge OF "SJ", `Senior Judge`, Date 5 1 2001
`an International Judge` MEANS Judge OF "IJ", `International Judge`, Date 6 1 2021

§§ `s 3: superior courts of record`

#ASSERT (`s 3 superior court of record: the court is declared a superior court of record` `General Division`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 3 superior court of record: the court is declared a superior court of record` `Appellate Division`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 3 superior court of record: the court is declared a superior court of record` `Court of Appeal`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A list that does not say "only": any other court is not covered.
#ASSERT (`s 3 superior court of record: the court is declared a superior court of record` `District Court`) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 3 superior court of record: the court is declared a superior court of record` `Singapore International Commercial Court`) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 3 superior court of record: the court is declared a superior court of record` `Family Division of the High Court`) EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 4: precedence`

-- Classes (a) to (f) in the order the section lists them; 0 for a Judge s 4 does not rank.
#ASSERT `s 4 the class of rank of the Judge, or 0 if s 4 does not rank the Judge` `the Chief Justice` EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `s 4 the class of rank of the Judge, or 0 if s 4 does not rank the Judge` `the earlier Vice-President` EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `s 4 the class of rank of the Judge, or 0 if s 4 does not rank the Judge` `the earlier Justice of the Court of Appeal` EQUALS 3
#ASSERT `s 4 the class of rank of the Judge, or 0 if s 4 does not rank the Judge` `the President of the Appellate Division` EQUALS 4
#ASSERT `s 4 the class of rank of the Judge, or 0 if s 4 does not rank the Judge` `an Appellate Division Judge` EQUALS 5
#ASSERT `s 4 the class of rank of the Judge, or 0 if s 4 does not rank the Judge` `an early High Court Judge` EQUALS 6
#ASSERT `s 4 the class of rank of the Judge, or 0 if s 4 does not rank the Judge` `a Judicial Commissioner` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `s 4 the class of rank of the Judge, or 0 if s 4 does not rank the Judge` `a Senior Judge` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `s 4 the class of rank of the Judge, or 0 if s 4 does not rank the Judge` `an International Judge` EQUALS 0

-- A higher class ranks before a lower one, and not the reverse (the Chief Justice, then the Vice-Presidents, then the other Justices, then the President of the AD, then its Judges, then the High Court).
#ASSERT (`s 4 the first Judge ranks before the second` `the Chief Justice` `the earlier Vice-President`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 4 the first Judge ranks before the second` `the earlier Vice-President` `the Chief Justice`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 4 the first Judge ranks before the second` `the later Vice-President` `the earlier Justice of the Court of Appeal`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 4 the first Judge ranks before the second` `the later Justice of the Court of Appeal` `the President of the Appellate Division`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 4 the first Judge ranks before the second` `the President of the Appellate Division` `an Appellate Division Judge`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 4 the first Judge ranks before the second` `a later Appellate Division Judge` `an early High Court Judge`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 4 the first Judge ranks before the second` `an early High Court Judge` `a later Appellate Division Judge`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Within a class, by the order of appointments.
#ASSERT (`s 4 the first Judge ranks before the second` `the earlier Vice-President` `the later Vice-President`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 4 the first Judge ranks before the second` `the later Vice-President` `the earlier Vice-President`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 4 the first Judge ranks before the second` `an early High Court Judge` `a later High Court Judge`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 4 the first Judge ranks before the second` `a later High Court Judge` `an early High Court Judge`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 4 the first Judge ranks before the second` `an Appellate Division Judge` `a later Appellate Division Judge`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Two Judges appointed on the same day: the Act does not order them.
#ASSERT (`s 4 the first Judge ranks before the second` `the earlier Justice of the Court of Appeal` `a Justice of the Court of Appeal appointed the same day`) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Two holders of the single office in (a): not ordered. A Judge s 4 does not rank: not covered.
#ASSERT (`s 4 the first Judge ranks before the second` `the Chief Justice` `another Chief Justice`) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 4 the first Judge ranks before the second` `a Judicial Commissioner` `an early High Court Judge`) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 4 the first Judge ranks before the second` `the Chief Justice` `an International Judge`) EQUALS NOTHING

-- The most senior of those sitting.
#ASSERT (`s 4 the most senior Supreme Court Judge among those sitting` (LIST `an early High Court Judge`, `an Appellate Division Judge`, `the earlier Justice of the Court of Appeal`)) EQUALS JUST `the earlier Justice of the Court of Appeal`
#ASSERT (`s 4 the most senior Supreme Court Judge among those sitting` (LIST `a later High Court Judge`, `an early High Court Judge`)) EQUALS JUST `an early High Court Judge`
#ASSERT (`s 4 the most senior Supreme Court Judge among those sitting` (LIST `the earlier Vice-President`, `the Chief Justice`, `the President of the Appellate Division`)) EQUALS JUST `the Chief Justice`
-- A Judicial Commissioner or Senior Judge in the list is passed over: s 4 ranks Supreme Court Judges.
#ASSERT (`s 4 the most senior Supreme Court Judge among those sitting` (LIST `a Senior Judge`, `a Judicial Commissioner`, `a later High Court Judge`)) EQUALS JUST `a later High Court Judge`
-- A tie at the top, an empty list, and a list with no ranked Judge: not covered.
#ASSERT (`s 4 the most senior Supreme Court Judge among those sitting` (LIST `the earlier Justice of the Court of Appeal`, `a Justice of the Court of Appeal appointed the same day`, `a later High Court Judge`)) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 4 the most senior Supreme Court Judge among those sitting` EMPTY) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 4 the most senior Supreme Court Judge among those sitting` (LIST `a Senior Judge`, `an International Judge`)) EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 5: acting appointment`

`the Vice-President is away` MEANS `s 5 Judge available to act` OF `the earlier Vice-President`, FALSE, TRUE
`the Chief Justice, present and able` MEANS `s 5 Judge available to act` OF `the Chief Justice`, TRUE, TRUE
`a Justice of the Court of Appeal, present and able` MEANS `s 5 Judge available to act` OF `the earlier Justice of the Court of Appeal`, TRUE, TRUE
`a High Court Judge, present and unable` MEANS `s 5 Judge available to act` OF `an early High Court Judge`, TRUE, FALSE
`a High Court Judge, present and able` MEANS `s 5 Judge available to act` OF `a later High Court Judge`, TRUE, TRUE

-- "Whenever ... the Chief Justice is unable": a "whenever" that is not met is a no.
#ASSERT (`s 5(1) the powers and duties of the Chief Justice pass to the next Judge in precedence` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 5(1) the powers and duties of the Chief Justice pass to the next Judge in precedence` FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The Judge with precedence next after the Chief Justice who is present and able: the Vice-President is away, so the Justice of the Court of Appeal.
#ASSERT (`s 5(1) the Judge who exercises the powers and duties of the Chief Justice` TRUE (LIST `the Chief Justice, present and able`, `the Vice-President is away`, `a High Court Judge, present and able`, `a Justice of the Court of Appeal, present and able`)) EQUALS JUST `the earlier Justice of the Court of Appeal`
-- No one present and able but a High Court Judge who is unable: no Judge named.
#ASSERT (`s 5(1) the Judge who exercises the powers and duties of the Chief Justice` TRUE (LIST `a High Court Judge, present and unable`, `the Vice-President is away`)) EQUALS NOTHING
-- The Chief Justice is not unable: the rule does not apply, so no Judge is named.
#ASSERT (`s 5(1) the Judge who exercises the powers and duties of the Chief Justice` FALSE (LIST `a Justice of the Court of Appeal, present and able`)) EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 5(2): a temporary absence in any part of Malaysia is not absence from Singapore.
#ASSERT (`s 5(2) the absence counts as absence from Singapore for s 5` TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 5(2) the absence counts as absence from Singapore for s 5` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 5A: International Judges`

`a sitting of the Singapore International Commercial Court` MEANS `s 5A sitting` OF `Singapore International Commercial Court`, FALSE, FALSE
`a sitting of the Court of Appeal on an appeal from the Singapore International Commercial Court` MEANS `s 5A sitting` OF `Court of Appeal`, TRUE, FALSE
`a sitting of the Appellate Division on an application relating to such an appeal` MEANS `s 5A sitting` OF `Appellate Division`, FALSE, TRUE
`a sitting of the General Division` MEANS `s 5A sitting` OF `General Division`, FALSE, FALSE
`a sitting of the Court of Appeal on another appeal` MEANS `s 5A sitting` OF `Court of Appeal`, FALSE, FALSE

#ASSERT (`s 5A an International Judge may sit in this sitting` `an International Judge` `a sitting of the Singapore International Commercial Court`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 5A an International Judge may sit in this sitting` `an International Judge` `a sitting of the Court of Appeal on an appeal from the Singapore International Commercial Court`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 5A an International Judge may sit in this sitting` `an International Judge` `a sitting of the Appellate Division on an application relating to such an appeal`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- "may only sit": anywhere else, no.
#ASSERT (`s 5A an International Judge may sit in this sitting` `an International Judge` `a sitting of the General Division`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 5A an International Judge may sit in this sitting` `an International Judge` `a sitting of the Court of Appeal on another appeal`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The section speaks of International Judges only.
#ASSERT (`s 5A an International Judge may sit in this sitting` `an early High Court Judge` `a sitting of the Singapore International Commercial Court`) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 5A an International Judge may sit in this sitting` `a Senior Judge` `a sitting of the General Division`) EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 7: vacations`

#ASSERT (`s 7 the vacations specified for the year are within the limit` 2) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 7 the vacations specified for the year are within the limit` 1) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 7 the vacations specified for the year are within the limit` 0) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- "must not exceed 2 months": three months is over the limit, and so is two and a bit.
#ASSERT (`s 7 the vacations specified for the year are within the limit` 3) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 7 the vacations specified for the year are within the limit` 2.5) EQUALS JUST FALSE
